1
00:00:00,216 --> 00:00:01,716
(sighs)

2
00:00:01,718 --> 00:00:03,988
(phone line ringing)

3
00:00:03,987 --> 00:00:06,087
(Dave(voice on phone):)Hello?
Hi, Dave.

4
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,389
(Amy:)Uh, it's Amy.

5
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:09,990
(Dave:)Oh. How are you?
I'm fine. How are you?

6
00:00:09,993 --> 00:00:13,023
(Dave:)Terrific. And pleasantly
surprised to hear from you,

7
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:15,559
(Dave:)given how I acted
on our last date.

8
00:00:15,565 --> 00:00:16,595
(Amy:)Yeah, well,

9
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:18,029
(Amy:)we both made mistakes, you know.

10
00:00:18,034 --> 00:00:21,004
(Amy:)I took the last breadstick,
you gushed over my ex-boyfriend

11
00:00:21,004 --> 00:00:25,204
(Amy:)like he was Leonard Nimoy
and you were my ex-boyfriend.

12
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:27,578
(Dave:)So, to what do I owe
the pleasure?

13
00:00:27,577 --> 00:00:29,507
(Amy:)Well, I was wondering

14
00:00:29,512 --> 00:00:32,242
(Amy:)if you'd like to get dinner
again sometime.

15
00:00:32,248 --> 00:00:33,878
(Dave:)Yes, please.

16
00:00:33,883 --> 00:00:36,753
(Sheldon(on phone):)Great.
Let me just check

17
00:00:36,753 --> 00:00:38,553
(Dave:)my schedule, he said,

18
00:00:38,555 --> 00:00:41,385
(Dave:)trying to seem like a man
with things on his schedule.

19
00:00:41,391 --> 00:00:43,691
(Amy:)How 'bout Saturday?

20
00:00:43,693 --> 00:00:45,063
(Dave:)Uh, hmm...

21
00:00:45,061 --> 00:00:46,561
(Dave:)Let me see. Uh, Friday,

22
00:00:46,563 --> 00:00:48,233
(Dave:)farmers' market with Jay Z.

23
00:00:48,231 --> 00:00:51,231
(Dave:)Sunday, piano shopping
with Elton John.

24
00:00:51,234 --> 00:00:52,904
(Dave:)Saturday works.

25
00:00:55,038 --> 00:00:58,538
(Raj:)Oh. Did you know,
at the United Nations,

26
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:01,241
(Raj:)there's a Department
for Outer Space Affairs?

